# Writing — go-live SEO

Writing pieces can ship at `/writing/[slug]` before they are linked from the main nav. When Writing is ready to promote on the site, do this SEO pass:

## Discovery + internal links

- Add Writing to main nav (`Nav.astro`) and footer if appropriate
- Add a Writing index (or clear entry points from home / About / CV) so crawlers and people can find pieces without relying on direct URLs
- Confirm CV and other internal links use the canonical `/writing/...` paths

## Per-piece metadata

- Every piece needs a strong `description` in frontmatter (used for meta + Article JSON-LD)
- Pass a dedicated social image into `Base` (lead figure JPG preferred — crawlers often skip AVIF). Set optional `image` + `imageAlt` in writing frontmatter; writing pages fall back to the sitewide OG image if omitted
- Keep `pubDate` accurate; Article schema already emits `datePublished`
- If the piece also lives on Medium (or elsewhere), decide canonical: prefer `art.adamsimms.xyz` as canonical when this is the primary home, and align Medium’s canonical / cross-post settings

## Site plumbing

- Sitemap already includes writing routes via `@astrojs/sitemap` — verify new slugs appear after build; only hide a piece if intentional (mirror `HIDDEN_PATHS` / `noindex` pattern used for work)
- After launch: request indexing in Search Console for `/writing` (or index) and key essays; spot-check rich results / OG previews (Facebook Sharing Debugger, Twitter/X card validator)

## Do not treat as done until

Nav (or index) links exist, each live essay has description + JPG OG image, and sitemap/Search Console have been checked.
